{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Consume</b> — sometimes 'little by little,' and in the end 'they are not.'" "And the sense of <b>he rules in Jacob</b> — since he mentioned <b>the Elohim of Israel</b>; and the meaning is that the elohim of the nations are idols, and the Elohim of Israel is a righteous judge."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:16.473510975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}